course: dictionary
lesson: 2840
title: Reading dm, the short way to write decimeter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: dm is a short way to write decimeter, a unit for measuring length. Writing dm saves space, just as cm is short for centimeter. «A log of 24 dm» means a log that is 24 decimeters long.
explain: Ten centimeters make one decimeter, so 1 dm = 10 cm. Ten decimeters make one meter, so 1 m = 10 dm. Each step up is ten times bigger.
explain: Read this sentence: «A log of 24 dm cut into pieces of 4 dm gives 24 ÷ 4 = 6 pieces, which takes 6 - 1 = 5 cuts.» Six pieces need only five cuts, because there is one cut between each pair of pieces, which is one fewer than the number of pieces.
fact: dm is short for decimeter. Some people spell it decimetre.
fact: 1 dm = 10 cm.
fact: 1 m = 10 dm.
fact: dm³ measures volume, and 1 dm³ = 1 liter.
fact: To find the cuts, count the pieces and take one away: 6 pieces need 5 cuts.
exercise: How many centimeters are in 1 dm? | 100 | 1000 | 1 | *10
exercise: «A rope is 30 dm long.» How many meters is that? | 30 m | *3 m | 300 m | 0.3 m
exercise: «A log of 24 dm cut into pieces of 4 dm gives 24 ÷ 4 = 6 pieces.» How many pieces is that? | *6 | 5 | 24 | 4
test: How many decimeters are in 1 m? | *10 | 1000 | 1 | 100
test: «A ribbon is 5 dm long.» How many centimeters is that? | 0.5 cm | 5 cm | *50 cm | 500 cm
exam: «A plank is 8 dm long and is cut into pieces of 2 dm.» How many cuts are needed? | *3 | 2 | 4 | 8
